# The old name, pointed at the new one.
#
# economyelite.com and standardnj.com were serving the same site independently,
# so Google treated them as two separate websites and kept ranking the old name
# above the new one. A 301 is permanent: it keeps every old link working and
# hands the trust the old domain built up over to standardnj.com instead of
# throwing it away.
#
# :splat carries the rest of the path through, so economyelite.com/policy.html
# lands on standardnj.com/policy.html rather than the home page.
#
# Keep renewing economyelite.com while these lines exist. If the domain lapses,
# the redirect dies with it and the old links go nowhere.

http://economyelite.com/*      https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!
https://economyelite.com/*     https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!
http://www.economyelite.com/*  https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!
https://www.economyelite.com/* https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!

# www to bare, so there is only ever one address for the new name too.
http://www.standardnj.com/*    https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!
https://www.standardnj.com/*   https://standardnj.com/:splat  301!
